+Concise Bounded Description
+--------------------------
+
+To extract everything a graph says about a resource, use
+:meth:`~rdflib.graph.Graph.cbd`. It returns a new
+:class:`~rdflib.graph.Graph` containing the *Concise Bounded
+Description* of the resource, as defined in the `W3C member submission
+<https://www.w3.org/Submission/CBD/>`_:
+
+1. Every triple whose subject is the resource is included.
+2. For every included triple whose object is a blank node, every triple
+   whose subject is that blank node is included too, recursively.
+
+Triples whose object is a URI are not followed, and incoming triples
+(where the resource is the object) are not included. Namespace bindings
+of the original graph are copied to the result::
+
+   from rdflib import Graph
+   from rdflib.namespace import Namespace
+
+   EX = Namespace("http://example.org/")
+   g = Graph().parse(data="""
+       @prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .
+       ex:a ex:name "A" ;
+            ex:addr [ ex:street "Main" ] .
+       ex:b ex:name "B" .
+       """, format="turtle")
+
+   described = g.cbd(EX.a)
+   # described contains:
+   #   ex:a ex:name "A"
+   #   ex:a ex:addr _:n
+   #   _:n  ex:street "Main"
+   # but not ex:b ex:name "B", as ex:b is a URI and is not followed.
+
+A resource of ``None`` gives an empty graph.
+
